          "weekPlanHtml": "<h3>Monday</h3><h3>Monday — Year in Review + Growth Reflection</h3><p>Facilitator Goal: Students see how far they have come — in their business and as people — and feel it.</p><h4>7:30–7:40 AM — Warm-Up: Week 1 vs. Now</h4><p>&quot;Think back to Week 1. What did you think entrepreneurship was then? What do you know now that you didn&#x27;t?&quot; 4-5 students share.</p><p>If you kept their Week 1 Entrepreneurial Identity sheets, hand them back now. The reactions are the whole point.</p><h4>7:40–8:15 AM — Year in Review Walk-Through</h4><p>Walk the class through the arc of the year, unit by unit. For each, students jot the biggest thing they built or learned:</p><p>Unit 1 (Weeks 1-6): mindset, your why, observing problems, first pitch</p><p>Unit 2 (Weeks 7-17): design thinking, customer discovery, MVP, sales, the final pitch</p><p>Unit 3 (Weeks 18-30): marketing, campaigns, and the finances</p><p>Unit 4 (Weeks 31-33): analytics, operations, and now — the recap</p><h4>8:15–8:50 AM — Growth Reflection</h4><p>Students write honestly about two kinds of growth:</p><p>Business growth — what is real now that did not exist in September (customers, sales, product, skills)</p><p>Personal growth — how they think, speak, or show up differently than they did in Week 1</p><p>&quot;The business might be big or small. That is not the point. The point is who you became by building it.&quot;</p><h4>8:50–9:00 AM — Close</h4><p>Preview: &quot;Tomorrow you gather the proof — the artifacts and numbers that tell your story.&quot;</p><h3>Tuesday</h3><h3>Tuesday — Evidence Gathering + Story Draft</h3><h4>7:30–7:35 AM — Warm-Up</h4><p>&quot;What is the single best piece of proof that your business is real?&quot; Around the room.</p><h4>7:35–8:10 AM — Evidence Gathering</h4><p>Students pull their strongest artifacts from the whole year into one place for the showcase: pitch deck, best campaign, sales/traction numbers, customer quotes, photos of product or events, dashboard.</p><p>&quot;You have been building this portfolio all year. Now you curate the highlights.&quot;</p><h4>8:10–8:45 AM — Year-End Story Draft</h4><p>Students draft their year-end story using a simple arc: where I started → what I built → what I learned → where I am headed.</p><p>&quot;This becomes the backbone of your showcase presentation in a few weeks. Get the honest version down now.&quot;</p><h4>8:45–9:00 AM — Speaker Tour Prep</h4><p>Distribute Speaker Tour Prep Worksheets.</p><h3>Wednesday</h3><h3>Wednesday — Speaker/Tour</h3><p>Run the speaker or tour per standard Wednesday format. Prompt: &quot;Ask the speaker what they wish they had known at the start of their journey.&quot;</p><h3>Thursday</h3><h3>Thursday — Speaker Recap + Thank You Cards + Portfolio Cleanup</h3><h4>7:30–7:35 AM — Warm-Up</h4><p>&quot;One sentence — most interesting thing from Wednesday.&quot; Around the room.</p><h4>7:35–7:55 AM — Speaker Recap</h4><p>Two columns: &quot;What we heard&quot; | &quot;What part of my year does this connect to?&quot;</p><h4>7:55–8:20 AM — Thank You Cards</h4><p>Handwritten. Specific. Required elements: one specific observation, one question it sparked, a genuine thank you.</p><h4>8:20–9:00 AM — Portfolio Cleanup</h4><p>Students organize their portfolio into a clean, presentable state for the showcase build. 1-on-1 focus: &quot;What is your strongest evidence, and what is the one-line version of your year?&quot;</p><h3>Friday</h3><h3>Friday — Profit or Broke + 1-on-1s + Showcase Preview</h3><h4>7:30–7:35 AM — Warm-Up</h4><p>&quot;One number that shows your progress this year.&quot; Around the room.</p><h4>7:35–8:00 AM — Profit or Broke (Week 33 — Rotation: Profit or Broke)</h4><p>Year-in-review edition: use real numbers from students&#x27; actual businesses this year. Celebrate the wins and treat the losses as lessons.</p><h4>8:00–8:35 AM — 1-on-1 Sessions</h4><p>1-on-1 focus: &quot;What are you most proud of this year? What is the story you want to tell at the showcase?&quot;</p><h4>8:35–8:55 AM — Showcase Preview</h4><p>Introduce the 3-week finale: Week 34 you build your brand + business snapshot, Week 35 you prep and rehearse, Week 36 is the Student Showcase — your businesses presented to family, community, and guests.</p><p>&quot;This is the finish line you have been running toward all year. Time to make it count.&quot;</p><h4>8:55–9:00 AM — Week Reflection</h4><p>One sentence each: &quot;The person I was in Week 1 vs. the person I am now.&quot;</p>"
